/* Modern theme for the system menu -- flat programmatic panel, matching login.rcss's modern
   translucent-dark-panel look. Buttons rely entirely on base.rcss's shared .btn.

   2026-09-03: #panel no longer C++-positioned/sized -- centered via base.rcss's .center-both
   utility class (applied in sys_menu.rml), fixed dp size matching CWinEx's own real geometry
   exactly (213 = the panel art's sprite width; 187/155 = TOP.height(64) + BOTTOM.height(43) +
   LEFT.texHeight(8) * 10-or-6 lines, SysMenuWin.cpp's SetLine() math -- 10 lines in the character
   scene, 6 in the login scene, toggled here via .compact rather than pushed from C++). Every
   button below is a fixed dp offset from the panel's own edges -- SetPosition()'s old per-button
   math (SMW_BTN_GAP=4, base offsets 33/height-52) is now baked into these numbers directly, no
   scene-awareness needed since exit-game/select-server anchor from the top and option/close
   anchor from the bottom (bottom-anchoring absorbs the .compact height difference for free). */
#panel {
	width: 213dp;
	height: 187dp;
	font-family: "Liberation Sans";
	font-size: 12px;
	color: white;
	background-color: rgba(26, 27, 29, 228);
	border: 1dp rgba(255, 255, 255, 30);
	border-radius: 10dp;
}
#panel.compact {
	height: 155dp;
}

#btn_exit_game    { left: 52dp; top: 33dp; }
#btn_select_server{ left: 52dp; top: 67dp; }
#btn_option       { left: 52dp; bottom: 86dp; }
#btn_close        { left: 52dp; bottom: 52dp; }
